{"title":"Career roadmap · Warehouse Manager","role":"Warehouse Manager","summary":"A Warehouse Manager plans and controls warehouse operations, inventory, receiving, storage, picking, packing, dispatch, workforce, safety, quality and warehouse technology. The role is central to modern supply-chain operations.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Com (Bachelor of Commerce)","Course":"B.Com – Logistics & Supply Chain"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"B.Com – Logistics & Supply Chain is strongly aligned, providing a foundation in commerce, inventory, logistics, procurement and supply-chain management."},{"type":"note","label":"Career-route check","text":"The target role is usually not the first job after graduation. A realistic route is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Com Logistics & Supply Chain","Logistics/Warehouse Intern","Warehouse Executive/Supervisor","Assistant Warehouse Manager","Warehouse Manager"]}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career objective"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Learn warehouse operations, inventory, ERP/WMS and logistics; enter as Warehouse/Logistics Executive"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Develop people-management, inventory-control and warehouse-technology expertise"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Become Warehouse Manager/Distribution Manager and manage larger facilities"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Progress toward Regional Warehouse, Distribution, Supply Chain or Operations leadership"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"text":"Commerce fundamentals"},{"text":"Accounting, economics, business"},{"text":"Business-process project"},{"text":"Business foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 2"},{"text":"Logistics basics"},{"text":"War